Frazil-Skronk

Ingredients: DANCE-PUNK & NU RAVE + FREE JAZZ / AVANT-GARDE + COZY, WARM & CHILL LO-FI + Hi-Hat + 1990s ERA
Creative Catalyst: It channels the acoustics of glacier caves melting in real time.

Frazil-Skronk sounds like an illegal 1997 rave staged inside an unstable blue ice vault, where hyperactive four-on-the-floor cowbell grooves and screeching, unhinged free-jazz saxophones collide with crackling, tape-decayed Rhodes chords and the rhythmic, hollow dripping of thawing permafrost. It is frenetic yet deeply insulated—a sweating, shivering clash between frantic physical kineticism and the muffled, dusty warmth of a battered four-track cassette recorder buried in wet snow.

