- Harmonic Palette: Diminished seventh and minor ninth jazz voicings coated in tape flutter, clashing violently against atonal brass multiphonics, blown-out acid bass octaves, and microtonal overtones tuned to resonant cavity acoustics.
- Production Signatures: 
  1. Cryo-Tape Smear: Master rhythm tracks are dumped onto damp, freezing Type-I cassette tapes played on misaligned heads, yielding a cozy, saturated midrange with random mechanical drag.
  2. Melt-Trigger Sidechain: Dynamic room microphones placed directly under thawing icicles trigger sharp ducking gates on synth basslines, making the groove surge every time a drop falls.
  3. Cavern Cavitation Delay: 1990s rackmount digital delays pushed to runaway feedback, equalized to replicate the sound of sound waves bouncing through hollowed-out, water-slicked blue ice tunnels.
- Dynamics: Abrupt volcanic shifts; a cozy, crackling lo-fi jazz vamp over soft hiss will suddenly rupture into an abrasive, glowstick-waving dance-punk tantrum of shrieking tenor sax and spitting cymbals, before dissolving into the solitary slosh of meltwater.

